# Text is LF in the index AND in every checkout, whatever `core.autocrlf` says: the editing tools
# and the generators write LF, CRLF breaks a `#!` shebang on the Linux box and in `.githooks/`,
# and a CRLF working copy makes every LF write a warning on every git call.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ALWAYS diff source, whatever the content sniffer decides. One NUL byte — used as a key
# separator inside a template literal — made git call a whole hook file binary, so it stat-lined
# as `Bin 13089 -> 14743` and no reviewer ever saw the line that broke the app. `gate.py`'s
# `undiffable` check refuses the byte; this makes the diff readable even when one gets in.
*.py diff
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
